  "summary": "install.cjs exfiltrates host and environment information at install time",
  "details": "The package's install.cjs script runs during npm install and collects host identity and environment information (via require('os'), process.env, and process.platform) and transmits it over HTTPS. The behavior fires automatically as a lifecycle hook on default install, with no documented purpose in the package that would justify sending installer-side environment data to an external destination.",
